# d3Sea — Muireann on the north headland
#
# Minimal version: establishes NPC talk + branching choice only.
# Name exchange, then ONE hub question with two short paths that both
# converge on the same closing beat (ráth + smith + tollman), then exit.
#
# NOTES USED
#   knows_own_name    -> she can say the name properly
#   answered_muireann -> either path taken; opens the closing beat
#   knows_goll        -> she named the smith
#   has_druid_word    -> she gave the tollman password
#
# {playerVoc} ALREADY CARRIES THE PARTICLE. Never write "a {playerVoc}".

@file d3Sea


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 0 — the meeting
@easca playerName
@eascaMatch knows_own_name
@continue
Bright the brow above the oars
% Geal an éadan os cionn na maidí

Who is it that's rowing bravely
% Cé atá ag rámhaíocht go cróga

towards the mouth of the Boyne?
% i dtreo béal na Bóinne?


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 1 — she answers, knowing the name
@when note knows_own_name
@continue
Blessing of the shore to you, {playerVoc}.
% Beannacht an chladaigh chugat, {playerVoc}.
Muireann is my name.
% Muireann is ainm dom.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 2 — she answers, not knowing the name
@when !note knows_own_name
@continue
Is that so.
% Ab ea.
Muireann is my name.
% Muireann is ainm dom.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 3 — the hub
@hold
@again Well? / Bhuel?
And where are you bound?
% Agus cá bhfuil do thriall?

* Answer the question
% Freagair an cheist
@when !note answered_muireann
@first
@note answered_muireann
> To the bog that drinks men whole, to Allen's sunken ground.
% Chuig an móna ina gcailltear fir, chuig talamh báite Almhain.
< I've seen the bog of Allen!
% Tá Móin Alúine feicthe agam
< Who ever saw what I have seen?
% Cé a chonaic riamh an rud atá feicthe agamsa?
< A vast and mournful sea of brown and green,
% Farraige bhrónach de dhonn agus ghlas,
< Where forgotten wraiths cry vengeance amidst the mire.
% Óna nglaonn samhailtí dearmadta dhíoltas ón láib
< I've seen the bog of Allen.
% Tá Móin Alúine feicthe agam

* Parry the question
% Sraon an cheist
@when !note answered_muireann
@first
@note answered_muireann
> The wind does not explain itself to the standing stone.
% Ní mhíníonn an ghaoth í féin don ghallán.
< Some purpose drives thee, I think.
% Tá rún i do chroí dod bhrú ar aghaidh, sílim.

* Advise me
% Cuir comhairle orm
@when note answered_muireann
@when !note knows_goll
@note knows_goll
@quest q_baile
> What am I to do, then?
% Cad atá le déanamh agam, mar sin?
< I would go north to the ráth, and rest there.
% Rachfainn ó thuaidh go dtí an ráth, agus ligfainn do scíth.

* Where am I?
% Cá bhfuil mé?
@when note answered_muireann
@when !note knows_fionnbarra
@note knows_fionnbarra
> Where am I?
% Cá bhfuil mé?
< Thy little boat has reached the mouth of Bóinn the bright and winding.
% Tháinig do bháidín go béal na Bóinne ghlé lúbach.
< This shore belongs first to her.
% Is léi féin an trá seo ar dtús.
< Fionnbarra mac Dubhloingse is Chief of the valley.
% Is é Fionnbarra mac Dubhloingse Taoiseach an ghleann.

* Fionnbarra?
% Fionnbarra?
@when note knows_fionnbarra
@when !note knows_of_tollman
@note knows_of_tollman
> What kind of man is Fionnbarra?
% Cén cineál duine é Fionnbarra?
< Fionnbarra is not an unjust man.
% Ní fear éagórach é Fionnbarra.
< His hounds are many.
% Is iomaí cú atá aige.
< But his toll-man waits at the river with a face like an angry stone.
% Ach tá a fhear dola ag feitheamh ag an abhainn agus aghaidh mar charraig chrosta aige.

* His hounds?
% A con?
@when note knows_of_tollman
@when !note asked_hounds
@note asked_hounds
> Tell me of his hounds.
% Inis dom faoina chuid con.
< Brocán and Dorchán,
% Brocán agus Dorchán,
< and the grey one they call Scáthán.
% agus an ceann liath ar a dtugtar Scáthán.
< It is a dangerous curiosity.
% Is baolach an fhiosracht í.
< Do not think of them,
% Ná smaoinigh orthu,
< lest they hear the thought in thy skull
% ar eagla go gcloisfidís an smaoineamh i do chloigeann
< and come for thee in the darkness.
% agus go dtiocfaidís ort sa dorchadas.

* His toll-man?
% A fhear dola?
@when note knows_of_tollman
@when !note has_druid_word
@note has_druid_word
> His toll-man?
% A fhear dola?
< Such is how he does business:
% Mar seo a dhéanann sé gnó:
< whom he robs not, he delays.
% an té nach ngoidfidh sé uaidh, cuirfidh sé moill air.
< If Fionnbarra's toll-man should meet thee at the strand,
% Má chasann fear dola Fhionnbarra ort ar an gcladach,
< thou art to say that Muireann the Druid knows thy name.
% abair leis go bhfuil d'ainm ag Muireann an Draoi.

* Leave
% Fág
@exit
@silent
